--------------------------------
multi modal processing pipeline.
---------------------------------
-Vision-Language Inference Loop :Mobile client captures image → uploads to Cloud Storage. triggers:
a. Pre-process with Sharp / OpenCV (denoise, crop).
b. OCR & layout parse (Gemini Vision or Document-AI).
c. Semantic chunking → embeddings → vector DB for future reuse.
Planner agent decides which grade levels need which output.
Generator agent uses extracted text + curriculum context to create differentiated worksheets (Gemini Pro multimodal)

-Multimodal Chain-of-Thought
Prompt Gemini to first describe salient regions, then reason over them, before generating pedagogy. This “multi-modal CoT” improves answer faithfulness for science diagrams or maps.

-Cross-Modal RAG
Store both image-patch embeddings and text embeddings in a single index; retrieval returns mixed modality evidence that is injected into the prompt, letting the LLM cite textbook figures alongside narrative

How This Stands Out:
By fusing multi-agent planning, self-reflection feedback loops, CoT-guided reasoning, and multimodal RAG grounding, your “Sahayak” behaves like a collaborative team of subject experts rather than a single black-box API caller—delivering culturally-relevant, syllabus-aligned outputs with verifiable sources and adaptive difficulty in real time.